{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "operations", "channel": "supply-chain-initiatives", "user": "david.chen", "message": "Team, quick update on the Lot code tracing infrastructure project. We're officially in early planning stages now. The feasibility study is underway and I need everyone's input.", "create_at": 1705420800000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "operations", "channel": "supply-chain-initiatives", "user": "maria.santos", "message": "Great to hear this is moving forward! We really need proper lot tracking for receiving, stocking, and especially for our prepared foods transformation processes. Current manual methods aren't scalable.", "create_at": 1705421100000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "operations", "channel": "supply-chain-initiatives", "user": "kevin.wu", "message": "I've been reviewing vendor options for the feasibility study. Looking at systems that can handle the full lifecycle - from receiving through to point of sale. Integration with our existing inventory system is the big challenge.", "create_at": 1705421400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "operations", "channel": "supply-chain-initiatives", "user": "jennifer.park", "message": "From a QA perspective, this is critical for our HACCP compliance. Tracing lot codes through our bakery and prepared foods departments would significantly improve our recall response capabilities.", "create_at": 1705421700000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "operations", "channel": "supply-chain-initiatives", "user": "david.chen", "message": "Agreed on all points. Current timeline has development kickoff projected for Q3 2024, but that's pending budget approval from executive leadership. The feasibility study results should help make our case.", "create_at": 1705422000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "operations", "channel": "supply-chain-initiatives", "user": "maria.santos", "message": "What's the scope looking like? All 50+ store locations from day one?", "create_at": 1705422300000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "operations", "channel": "supply-chain-initiatives", "user": "kevin.wu", "message": "Feasibility study is evaluating a phased rollout - likely starting with BC locations before expanding to U.S. stores. FDA and CFIA have slightly different requirements we need to account for.", "create_at": 1705422600000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "operations", "channel": "supply-chain-initiatives", "user": "david.chen", "message": "Exactly. Let's target having the feasibility report finalized by end of February. That gives us time for budget discussions before Q2 planning. @jennifer.park can you document the QA requirements by next week?", "create_at": 1705422900000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "operations", "channel": "supply-chain-initiatives", "user": "jennifer.park", "message": "Will do. I'll include our current gap analysis and projected compliance benefits.", "create_at": 1705423200000}}

