{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "marcus.chen", "email": "marcus.chen@leesmarket.com", "password": "Pr@Research99", "teams": [{"name": "corporate-comms", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "diana.patel", "email": "diana.patel@leesmarket.com", "password": "C0mms#2023!", "teams": [{"name": "corporate-comms", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "kevin.nakamura", "email": "kevin.nakamura@leesmarket.com", "password": "Nakamura$PR1", "teams": [{"name": "corporate-comms", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Hey team, I finally compiled the Q4 2022 survey results comparing employee vs public perception. We need to discuss this before it goes to leadership.", "create_at": 1684940400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "jennifer.wong", "message": "Great, what are we looking at?", "create_at": 1684940520000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "So here's the concern - on the internal survey, only 42% of our employees agreed that Lee's Market 'is an ethical alternative to large retailers.' But 58% of the general public agreed on the parallel external survey we ran.", "create_at": 1684940700000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "diana.patel", "message": "Wait, so the public thinks we're MORE ethical than our own employees do? That's... not great.", "create_at": 1684940880000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "kevin.nakamura", "message": "That's a 16 point gap. Employees see the day-to-day operations. They know things customers don't.", "create_at": 1684941000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "jennifer.wong", "message": "This is concerning. We position ourselves as the ethical alternative to big box stores, but if our own people don't buy it, that messaging rings hollow.", "create_at": 1684941180000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Exactly. I think we need to loop in HR. Maybe there are specific pain points - wages, scheduling, supplier practices - that are driving this perception internally.", "create_at": 1684941360000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "diana.patel", "message": "Agreed. We can't just fix this with better messaging. If employees across our 5000+ workforce feel this way, there's something real underneath.", "create_at": 1684941540000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "jennifer.wong", "message": "Let's set up a meeting with HR leadership next week. Marcus, can you prep a summary deck? We need to address this gap before it becomes a bigger issue.", "create_at": 1684941720000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "corporate-comms", "channel": "pr-research", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "On it. I'll have something ready by Thursday.", "create_at": 1684941840000}}

