{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "sustainability", "channel": "carbon-transparency", "user": "jennifer.wu", "message": "Hey team, I've been going through the 2024 sustainability report and wanted to discuss the carbon footprint transparency reception. Has everyone had a chance to look at the customer perception data?", "create_at": 1706356800000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "sustainability", "channel": "carbon-transparency", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Yeah, just finished reviewing it. Pretty interesting findings tbh. The Canada vs U.S. split was notable.", "create_at": 1706357100000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "sustainability", "channel": "carbon-transparency", "user": "david.tran", "message": "I think so too. Afaik, Canadian customers were moderately more positive about our transparency efforts. The report showed around 76% reported positive influence in Canada compared to like 68% in the U.S. markets.", "create_at": 1706357400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "sustainability", "channel": "carbon-transparency", "user": "priya.sharma", "message": "That tracks with what I've been hearing from our U.S. store managers. Customers appreciate it but I think there's still some skepticism about corporate sustainability claims in general down here.", "create_at": 1706357700000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "sustainability", "channel": "carbon-transparency", "user": "jennifer.wu", "message": "Makes sense. The 8% gap isn't huge but it's worth understanding. @marcus.chen any theories on why Canadian markets responded better?", "create_at": 1706358000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "sustainability", "channel": "carbon-transparency", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Last I heard, Canadian consumers generally have higher baseline trust in sustainability messaging. Plus our Richmond HQ probably helps - customers see us as more locally accountable there.", "create_at": 1706358300000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "sustainability", "channel": "carbon-transparency", "user": "david.tran", "message": "Pretty sure it also relates to regulatory environment. Canada has stricter labeling standards so customers might be more accustomed to trusting those claims.", "create_at": 1706358600000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "sustainability", "channel": "carbon-transparency", "user": "priya.sharma", "message": "Should we consider tailoring our messaging for U.S. markets? Maybe more third-party verification messaging?", "create_at": 1706358900000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "sustainability", "channel": "carbon-transparency", "user": "jennifer.wu", "message": "Good idea. Let's schedule a deeper dive next week. I'll pull together some recommendations based on these findings.", "create_at": 1706359200000}}

