{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "david.chen", "message": "Hey team, just wrapped up reviewing the March 2027 patient questionnaire results. We need to discuss some concerning findings about Q1 satisfaction scores.", "create_at": 1736438400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "rachel.thompson", "message": "Oh no, what came up? I thought we were doing better this quarter.", "create_at": 1736438520000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "david.chen", "message": "So the data shows patients who contacted support with billing confusion rated their experience only 2.1/5 on average. Compare that to 4.8/5 for patients who didn't need any post-visit clarification. Pretty stark difference.", "create_at": 1736438700000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "lisa.patel", "message": "Wow that's a huge gap. I think this might be related to how we're communicating next steps after consultations? Patients seem confused about billing particularly.", "create_at": 1736438880000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "marcus.wu", "message": "I'm pretty sure we've seen this pattern before. When agents take time to clearly explain billing during support calls, scores could be climbing to around 3.6/5. Still not ideal but much better.", "create_at": 1736439060000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "rachel.thompson", "message": "That 3.6 score is interesting - clear explanations definitely help. Maybe we should implement mandatory billing explanation protocols for all support interactions?", "create_at": 1736439240000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "david.chen", "message": "Good thinking. The questionnaire results suggest post-visit confusion about billing and next steps is really hurting our overall CSAT. We need proactive communication, not just reactive support.", "create_at": 1736439420000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "lisa.patel", "message": "I can draft some updated scripts for the team. Should include billing breakdown and clear next steps for every patient interaction.", "create_at": 1736439600000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "marcus.wu", "message": "Sounds great Lisa. Let's also consider sending automated billing summaries after each virtual consultation. Might prevent a lot of these support calls in the first place.", "create_at": 1736439780000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "customer-experience", "channel": "patient-satisfaction", "user": "david.chen", "message": "Perfect. Let's sync tomorrow to finalize the action plan. Thanks everyone! \ud83d\ude4f", "create_at": 1736439900000}}

