Best regards,
Rachel", "folder": "sent", "read": true, "attachments": []}
{"type": "email", "id": "email_002", "subject": "Re: Improving Patient Access to Virtual Services", "from": "michael.johnson@mediconn.com", "from_name": "Michael Johnson", "to": ["rachel.lee@mediconn.com"], "cc": ["lisa.campbell@mediconn.com", "peter.murphy@mediconn.com", "sarah.brown@mediconn.com", "james.miller@mediconn.com", "karen.davis@mediconn.com", "david.martin@mediconn.com"], "date": "2026-01-05 10:15:00", "body": "Hi Rachel,

I agree that improving patient access should be a priority. A good starting point would be to evaluate the effectiveness of our current tools in managing customer interactions. If I recall correctly, back in 2024, we used Zendesk for ticket management, RingCentral for phone systems, Salesforce for CRM, and Slack for internal team communication. These tools were integrated with our proprietary patient platform through API connections.

Maybe we could explore how to optimize these tools further or consider new technologies that can help us provide a smoother online experience for our patients.

Regards,
Michael", "folder": "sent", "read": true, "attachments": []}
{"type": "email", "id": "email_003", "subject": "Re: Improving Patient Access to Virtual Services", "from": "rachel.lee@mediconn.com", "from_name": "Rachel Lee", "to": ["michael.johnson@mediconn.com"], "cc": ["lisa.campbell@mediconn.com", "peter.murphy@mediconn.com", "sarah.brown@mediconn.com", "james.miller@mediconn.com", "karen.davis@mediconn.com", "david.martin@mediconn.com"], "date": "2026-01-05 11:00:00", "body": "Hi Michael,

