{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "clinical-ops", "channel": "prescribing-tools", "user": "dr.nina.patel", "message": "Hey team, quick question - I was chatting with someone from the Vancouver office and they mentioned something about our reference materials system. Anyone know how the centralized platform is actually helping with prescribing decisions?", "create_at": 1741012800000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "clinical-ops", "channel": "prescribing-tools", "user": "james.whitmore", "message": "Good timing @dr.nina.patel. I was just reviewing this with the platform team last week. So afaik, the internal system consolidates all the clinical references, guidelines, and educational resources into one place. Makes it way easier than hunting through multiple databases.", "create_at": 1741013100000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "clinical-ops", "channel": "prescribing-tools", "user": "dr.sarah.chen", "message": "That's been my experience too. Last I heard from Marcus, everything gets updated monthly by the platform team. Having everything centralized really reduces the risk of using outdated dosing info or contraindication lists.", "create_at": 1741013400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "clinical-ops", "channel": "prescribing-tools", "user": "marcus.okonkwo", "message": "Yep, can confirm. We push updates monthly - usually around the 15th. The idea is that clinicians shouldn't have to jump between external sites or wonder if they're looking at current guidelines. Everything from drug interactions to provincial formulary changes is right there.", "create_at": 1741013700000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "clinical-ops", "channel": "prescribing-tools", "user": "dr.nina.patel", "message": "That's really helpful. I think one of the new locums was asking about this yesterday - she wanted to verify a pediatric dosing reference and wasn't sure where to look.", "create_at": 1741014000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "clinical-ops", "channel": "prescribing-tools", "user": "james.whitmore", "message": "Point her to the unified dashboard. It's designed to support safe prescribing by giving everyone access to the same vetted materials. Reduces variability and potential errors significantly.", "create_at": 1741014300000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "clinical-ops", "channel": "prescribing-tools", "user": "dr.sarah.chen", "message": "Exactly. Having that single source of truth is huge for patient safety. No more wondering if you're looking at the right version of a clinical guideline. \ud83d\udc4d", "create_at": 1741014600000}}

