{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "ota-security-updates", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Hey team, quick sync on our 2026 proactive security OTA roadmap. We need to finalize numbers for the board presentation next week.", "create_at": 1737460800000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "ota-security-updates", "user": "priya.sharma", "message": "Sure thing. From what I've seen in the draft plan, we're looking at somewhere around 10 proactive OTA updates for cyber threat mitigation across all models in 2026. Could be slightly less though.", "create_at": 1737461100000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "ota-security-updates", "user": "derek.williams", "message": "I think the number might be closer to 8 actually. That's what the initial planning doc mentioned. Still a big jump from our 2025 efforts where we only pushed 4 proactive updates.", "create_at": 1737461400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "ota-security-updates", "user": "lisa.nguyen", "message": "Derek's right. The 2025 baseline was 4 proactive OTAs. Doubling that to 8 for 2026 aligns with our ISO 26262 compliance goals and the new threat landscape we're seeing.", "create_at": 1737461700000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "ota-security-updates", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Good catch. So the initial plan targets 8 proactive security-focused OTA updates for 2026. That covers the EX-4, EX-7, and the new plug-in hybrid line?", "create_at": 1737462000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "ota-security-updates", "user": "priya.sharma", "message": "Yep, various models across the fleet. The increased frequency should help us stay ahead of emerging threats rather than just reacting to them.", "create_at": 1737462300000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "ota-security-updates", "user": "derek.williams", "message": "Exactly. Proactive measures are key. Last year's 4 updates were decent but leadership wanted more aggressive prevention. 8 updates feels like the right step up.", "create_at": 1737462600000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "ota-security-updates", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Perfect. I'll confirm 8 proactive OTAs in the presentation. Thanks everyone!", "create_at": 1737462900000}}

