{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "portal-updates", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Hey team, quick update on the 2026 roadmap. We're targeting the third week of March for our first major portal update next year.", "create_at": 1735550400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "portal-updates", "user": "diana.reyes", "message": "Nice! What's the main focus for that release?", "create_at": 1735550520000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "portal-updates", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Big one - we're finally moving away from SMS for 2FA. Afaik, the plan is to require hardware security keys for all customer portal logins.", "create_at": 1735550700000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "portal-updates", "user": "kevin.omalley", "message": "About time tbh. SMS verification has been a weak point for a while now. SIM swapping attacks have been on the rise.", "create_at": 1735550880000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "portal-updates", "user": "priya.sharma", "message": "So just to confirm - hardware security keys will be mandatory? No SMS option at all after the update?", "create_at": 1735551000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "portal-updates", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Correct. Last I heard from compliance, SMS verification will no longer be accepted as an available 2FA method due to security reasons. Users will need to add a hardware key as part of the authentication process.", "create_at": 1735551180000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "portal-updates", "user": "diana.reyes", "message": "We should probably start working on customer communications now. That's a significant change and people will need time to get their keys.", "create_at": 1735551300000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "portal-updates", "user": "kevin.omalley", "message": "Agreed. Should we partner with a hardware key vendor for discounts? Might ease the transition for customers.", "create_at": 1735551480000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "cybersecurity", "channel": "portal-updates", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Good idea Kevin. I'll bring that up in the next planning meeting. Let's make this transition as smooth as possible for our Elexion customers.", "create_at": 1735551600000}}

