{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "derek.huang", "email": "derek.huang@elexion.com", "password": "Pr0cure$2026!", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "maria.santos", "email": "maria.santos@elexion.com", "password": "SupplyM@nager1", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user team_admin"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "kyle.brennan", "email": "kyle.brennan@elexion.com", "password": "RiskAn@lyst99", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "jennifer.wu", "email": "jennifer.wu@elexion.com", "password": "F1nance2026$", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "maria.santos", "message": "Hey team, wanted to kick off a discussion about our lithium supplier situation. We've got the quarterly risk review coming up and I need to consolidate our findings.", "create_at": 1711699200000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "derek.huang", "message": "Good timing. I've been looking at this actually. So we currently work with five lithium suppliers, and I'm pretty sure all of them operate under annual fixed-pricing clauses tied to regional contract rates.", "create_at": 1711699500000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "kyle.brennan", "message": "That's what I have too. The fixed-pricing structure might be an issue if lithium spot prices drop significantly. We'd be locked in at higher rates for the contract period.", "create_at": 1711699800000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "jennifer.wu", "message": "From finance's perspective, this could be a concern. If competitors negotiate more flexible terms, our cost basis might not be competitive.", "create_at": 1711700100000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "maria.santos", "message": "Right, and having all five suppliers with similar pricing mechanisms means we don't really have diversification in our contract structures. That's a concentration risk.", "create_at": 1711700400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "derek.huang", "message": "I think the regional rate tie-ins could be problematic too. If one region experiences supply disruptions, we might see cascading price adjustments across multiple suppliers simultaneously.", "create_at": 1711700700000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "kyle.brennan", "message": "Exactly. It might be worth exploring spot-market options for a portion of our volume? Could hedge against the fixed-price exposure.", "create_at": 1711701000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "maria.santos", "message": "Good suggestion. Let's document these risks for the review. I'll draft a summary highlighting the supplier mix concentration and pricing structure vulnerabilities.", "create_at": 1711701300000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "jennifer.wu", "message": "Sounds good. I can pull together some scenario modeling on potential cost impacts by EOW.", "create_at": 1711701600000}}

