{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "marcus.chen", "email": "marcus.chen@elexion.com", "password": "Pr0cure2025!", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "diana.ross", "email": "diana.ross@elexion.com", "password": "SupplyMgr#25", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user team_admin"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "kevin.patel", "email": "kevin.patel@elexion.com", "password": "RiskAnalyst99!", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "lisa.nguyen", "email": "lisa.nguyen@elexion.com", "password": "Finance2025#", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "diana.ross", "message": "Team, I need us to review our lithium supplier situation before the Q1 executive briefing next week. @marcus.chen can you put together a risk summary?", "create_at": 1737640800000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Sure Diana. Quick overview: Elexion relies on three suppliers for lithium \u2014 LithiumCore, Atacama Minerals, and PacRim Resources. All three operate under semi-annual fixed-pricing agreements based on our 2024 contract terms.", "create_at": 1737641400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "kevin.patel", "message": "That concentration concerns me. Three suppliers isn't much diversification, especially with how volatile lithium spot prices have been lately.", "create_at": 1737642000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Agreed. The fixed-pricing gives us cost predictability through H1, but if any supplier faces disruption, we have limited backup options. Plus when renegotiation comes in July, we could see significant price adjustments.", "create_at": 1737642600000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "lisa.nguyen", "message": "From finance perspective, the semi-annual pricing structure helped our 2024 margins, but it also means we're exposed to market swings twice a year. What's the contingency if one supplier defaults?", "create_at": 1737643200000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "kevin.patel", "message": "We'd be scrambling honestly. Lead time to qualify a new lithium supplier is 4-6 months minimum given our quality requirements for battery cells.", "create_at": 1737643800000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "diana.ross", "message": "Let's recommend adding 1-2 backup suppliers to the qualified list this year. @marcus.chen include that in your risk summary along with cost projections. We need to present this proactively to leadership.", "create_at": 1737644400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Will do. I'll have the full risk assessment document ready by tomorrow afternoon.", "create_at": 1737645000000}}

