{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "marcus.chen", "email": "marcus.chen@elexion.com", "password": "Pr0cure#2026!", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "diana.patel", "email": "diana.patel@elexion.com", "password": "D!ana$ecure99", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user team_admin"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "jorge.reyes", "email": "jorge.reyes@elexion.com", "password": "J0rge#Supply24", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "user", "user": {"username": "karen.mills", "email": "karen.mills@elexion.com", "password": "K@ren2026!Fin", "teams": [{"name": "supply-chain", "roles": "team_user"}]}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "diana.patel", "message": "Hey team, wanted to get your thoughts on our lithium supplier situation. Leadership is asking for a risk summary by end of week.", "create_at": 1714729200000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "Sure thing. So I'm pretty sure we're currently sourcing from four suppliers total. That's been our setup for the past couple years.", "create_at": 1714729500000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "jorge.reyes", "message": "Yeah that's right. The thing that might be concerning is how those contracts are structured. I think they all have annual fixed-pricing clauses tied to regional contract markets.", "create_at": 1714729800000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "karen.mills", "message": "From a finance perspective, that could be a double-edged sword. Fixed pricing gives us predictability but if market rates drop significantly we're locked in at higher prices.", "create_at": 1714730100000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "diana.patel", "message": "Right, and conversely if there's a supply crunch we might be somewhat protected. What about geographic concentration?", "create_at": 1714730400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "marcus.chen", "message": "That's where things could be tricky. The regional contract markets they're tied to means if one region faces disruption, those suppliers might all adjust similarly.", "create_at": 1714730700000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "jorge.reyes", "message": "I think so too. Four suppliers sounds diversified but the annual pricing reset creates exposure. If lithium spot prices swing wildly between renewals we have limited flexibility to respond.", "create_at": 1714731000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "karen.mills", "message": "Should we recommend exploring shorter-term hedging instruments or maybe adding a fifth supplier with different contract terms?", "create_at": 1714731300000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "supply-chain", "channel": "procurement-risk", "user": "diana.patel", "message": "Good ideas. Let's compile this into the risk report. I'll draft something up and share it tomorrow for review. Thanks everyone!", "create_at": 1714731600000}}

